Define a raising operator $a_+$ that moves a state up one level and a lowering operator $a_-$ that moves it down one level: $\begin{aligned}
a_+|n\rangle &= \sqrt{n+1}\,|n+1\rangle,\\
a_-|n\rangle &= \sqrt{n}\,|n-1\rangle.\end{aligned}$ The numerical square-root factors are part of the definitions. On the lowest state, $a_-|0\rangle=0,$ because there is no state below the ground state.

